  "generated_text": "1. We know that the sum of the angles around a point is \\(360^\\circ\\).\n2. In the given figure, we have three angles: \\(160^\\circ\\), \\(x^\\circ\\), and \\(x^\\circ\\).\n3. Therefore, the sum of these angles must equal \\(360^\\circ\\).\n\nSo, we can write the equation:\n\\[ 160^\\circ + x^\\circ + x^\\circ = 360^\\circ \\]\n\n4. Simplify the equation by combining like terms:\n\\[ 160^\\circ + 2x^\\circ = 360^\\circ \\]\n\n5. Subtract \\(160^\\circ\\) from both sides:\n\\[ 2x^\\circ = 360^\\circ - 160^\\circ \\]\n\\[ 2x^\\circ = 200^\\circ \\]\n\n6. Divide both sides by 2:\n\\[ x^\\circ = \\frac{200^\\circ}{2} \\]\n\\[ x^\\circ = 100^\\circ \\]\n\n\\boxed{1}",
